# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep host-built
# artefacts out of the image.
#
# The frontend stage runs `npm ci` and then `COPY frontend/ ./`. Without this
# file that COPY would drop the host's node_modules over the ones just
# installed inside the container. On a Windows or macOS host those contain
# platform-specific esbuild and rollup binaries, and the vite build then fails
# with "Cannot find module @rollup/rollup-linux-x64-gnu". CI never hit this
# because a fresh checkout has no node_modules, but every local `make build`
# would.

# Node
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
.vite

# Python
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/htmlcov
**/.coverage

# Build output and packaging artefacts
build/
dist/
*.spk
*.tar

# Runtime data and secrets: these must never enter an image layer
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.env
.env.local
*.p8
apple_user_token.json
settings.json
secrets.json
**/_dev*

# VCS, CI and docs that the image does not need
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.editorconfig
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/desktop.ini
